* Exact status codes per key, with a "_upstream" suffix when a proxied
  request got no status from its last upstream attempt (e.g. 499_upstream):
  "status_codes" field, nginx_reqstat_status_codes_total metric
* New: req_status_show_format json, exact status codes per key
* New: req_status_show_key, to show a single key (404 if unknown)

* Sync with the latest Tengine reqstat module (tengine 3.x):
  - detailed status codes: http_200, 206, 302, 304, 403, 404, 416, 499,
    500, 502, 503, 504, 508, http_other_detail_status
  - upstream status: http_ups_4xx, http_ups_5xx
  - directives req_status_show_field, req_status_bypass, req_status_lazy,
    req_status_zone_add_indicator, req_status_zone_key_length,
    req_status_zone_recycle
  - recycling of rarely used keys when a zone is full
  - statistics follow internal redirects
  - dynamic module support
* New: req_status_show_format prometheus
* Works with stock nginx (tested 1.18 - 1.31), connection.patch is no longer
  needed: bytes_in is $request_length, bytes_out is $bytes_sent
* conn_total counts connections, not streams, for HTTP/2 and HTTP/3
* Fixes over upstream: keys hidden from output when their first request was
  not the first on a connection; bytes_out over-counted for requests finalized
  before the rewrite phase; key truncation/lookup mismatch; crash on
  "req_status_zone" with too few arguments; crash when the zone is too small
  to hold any key; memory corruption when key length changed on reload;
  division by zero in req_status_zone_recycle; status page sending headers
  before the body could be built

* Patched to work with nginx
* Initial check in, forked from tengine 2.1.0
